# Semgrep ignore list (maruda harness).
# NOTE: creating this file replaces Semgrep's built-in default ignores,
# so the common ones are restated below.
#
# Policy: Semgrep is a HARD GATE. When a false positive appears, exclude
# the smallest possible unit (a single file, or better: an inline
# `# nosemgrep: <rule-id>` with a reason). Never exclude whole source
# directories — that bypasses the SAST gate.
.git/
:include .gitignore
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
vendor/
.venv/
# Semgrep rule fixtures: .semgrep/ holds custom rules next to their
# `semgrep --test` fixtures, which are intentionally vulnerable test code.
# This excludes rule fixtures only — never application source.
.semgrep/
